            {
                "entry_id": "7a393815-6b65-3c9d-a8e4-ef25f1f98fdc",
                "word": "agonistique",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "cdb6096e-fee7-428d-9d52-b8e0e97991c9",
                        "entry_id": "7a393815-6b65-3c9d-a8e4-ef25f1f98fdc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "agonistiques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "afb1121b-6404-3d30-92f4-d6dd5bca732f",
                        "entry_id": "7a393815-6b65-3c9d-a8e4-ef25f1f98fdc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Partie de la gymnastique qui avait rapport aux combats et où les athlètes luttaient tous armés."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Gymnastique"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "912fa7fd-43c5-4555-9048-b3048a7dc6f4",
                                "sense_id": "afb1121b-6404-3d30-92f4-d6dd5bca732f",
                                "text": "La gymnastique et l’agonistique y tenaient, en somme, très peu de place. On était loin de l’époque héroïque de Romulus et des premières années de la République."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "90bef698-53ac-4215-91b1-fa1957e9635e",
                        "source_entry_id": "7a393815-6b65-3c9d-a8e4-ef25f1f98fdc",
                        "source_sense_id": "afb1121b-6404-3d30-92f4-d6dd5bca732f",
                        "target_lang_word": "agonistic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "agonistic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d3347be9-ce84-37f5-bf1b-a61b96c8c0cf",
                                        "entry_id": "3e4a32d6-6a9a-3b7b-8f9a-d85c9477bc31",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to contests that were originally participated in by the Ancient Greeks; athletic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4d10733-db99-499d-86d9-342bf96bd00d",
                                                "sense_id": "d3347be9-ce84-37f5-bf1b-a61b96c8c0cf",
                                                "text": "These words, with what follow, are for the most part agonistic, referring to the customes of the Grecian exercices, in their games. The words [translated] apprehended, signifie to catch, or apprehend the Crown, that hung over the Goal: so also [the word translated] perfect, is an Agonistic word that signifies the being crowned, or receiving the reward:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80cd7e2e-f79e-43e8-828c-9302dac24e8a",
                                                "sense_id": "d3347be9-ce84-37f5-bf1b-a61b96c8c0cf",
                                                "text": "Joys of the solitary walk, the spirit bow’d yet proud, the suffering and the struggle?\nThe agonistic throes, the ecstasies, joys of the solemn musings day or night?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4107aa88-740f-33d6-84aa-3a14e3700ac8",
                                        "entry_id": "3e4a32d6-6a9a-3b7b-8f9a-d85c9477bc31",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Characterised by conflict or hostility."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "891d906e-a380-4a4b-b019-ad8db4c3daf0",
                                                "sense_id": "4107aa88-740f-33d6-84aa-3a14e3700ac8",
                                                "text": "Although most agonistic interactions consist of signals of threat and submission, symbolic aggression is effective only because the possibility of escalation exists […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24760230-afba-46de-aa55-1f2a6d73e1d4",
                                                "sense_id": "4107aa88-740f-33d6-84aa-3a14e3700ac8",
                                                "text": "This was clearly such an event, but like the ancient religion of Israel, it was also deeply agonistic."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc87fdd2-c805-4de6-ac38-141631f04447",
                                                "sense_id": "4107aa88-740f-33d6-84aa-3a14e3700ac8",
                                                "text": "Sociality swung wildly between extremes of collective affiliation and agonistic striving for dominance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4bb64dd9-e258-3125-b273-0e8e1515a6e3",
                                        "entry_id": "3e4a32d6-6a9a-3b7b-8f9a-d85c9477bc31",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Argumentative; combative."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rhetoric"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "165bbbe8-cc46-4915-be19-05983d3a466c",
                                                "sense_id": "4bb64dd9-e258-3125-b273-0e8e1515a6e3",
                                                "text": "Sharply Frank said, “A place like this is a crimp in your plan, isn’t it?”\nBoone’s gaze returned to him. The surrounding crowd slipped away, sensing the agonistic nature of the exchange."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "58adcb73-dc74-3671-a1b8-c575aa3969b0",
                                        "entry_id": "3e4a32d6-6a9a-3b7b-8f9a-d85c9477bc31",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Struggling to achieve an effect; strained and contrived."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4c97f760-3d00-389e-ae29-a3f17b030579",
                                        "entry_id": "3e4a32d6-6a9a-3b7b-8f9a-d85c9477bc31",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to an agonist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
